// 014.3 (T23): a valid prospective `Amend` updates rules for future transactions without
// retroactively extinguishing an already-accrued escrow obligation, and void `Amend`s
// lacking quorum/timelock leave the active rule set unchanged. Also checks eFLINT atoms.
Fact legacy-amend-atoms Identified by Amend, Repeals, Installs, Protects, Entrenched, Regime.

Fact board Identified by Board1.
Fact depositor Identified by Alice, Bob.
Fact custodian Identified by Cust1.
Fact quorum Identified by board.
Fact timelock-ready Identified by board.
Fact escrow-settled Identified by depositor.

Duty refund-escrow Holder custodian Claimant depositor
  Violated when Held(refund-escrow(custodian, depositor)) For 10.

Power open-escrow Actor depositor Related to custodian
  Holds when True
  Valid when True
  Creates refund-escrow(custodian, depositor).

Amend suspend-new-escrows Actor board
  Repeals open-escrow
  Holds when quorum(board)
  Valid when quorum(board) && timelock-ready(board).

Scenario prospective-amend-preserves-active-escrow {
  // Alice opens escrow at t = 0 under LawVersion 0:
  open-escrow(Alice, Cust1).
  ?refund-escrow(Cust1, Alice).
  @ 3.
  // Attempt Amend before quorum + timelock -> void, open-escrow still valid!
  ?!valid suspend-new-escrows(Board1).
  suspend-new-escrows(Board1).
  ?valid open-escrow(Bob, Cust1).
  // Establish quorum + timelock -> valid Amend repeals prospective `open-escrow`:
  +quorum(Board1).
  +timelock-ready(Board1).
  ?valid suspend-new-escrows(Board1).
  suspend-new-escrows(Board1).
  // Alice's already-accrued `refund-escrow` duty remains in force with its t = 0 timestamp!
  ?refund-escrow(Cust1, Alice).
  ?!violated refund-escrow(Cust1, Alice).
  @ 10.
  ?violated refund-escrow(Cust1, Alice).
}
